{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And He brought near, etc.</b> One needs to know what is the separation that He spoke of in the preceding verse, and what is the bringing near that He speaks of here? Perhaps He intended two levels: the first is the separation of the tribe of Levi from the congregation of Israel in a general sense, and corresponding to this He said <b>for He separated</b>, etc., <b>from the congregation of Israel</b>; and the second is the bringing near of the sons of Kehat — that He brought them nearer than the rest of the Levites to bear the holy of holies. And see what I explained in the verse (Numbers 4:2) ״נָשֹׂא אֶת רֹאשׁ בְּנֵי קְהָת״, and corresponding to this He said <b>and He brought you near, and all your brothers</b>, meaning the branch of the Kehatites, the sons of Levi. And He was precise to say <b>you</b> — He hinted to him that all of them depend upon him and he is the greatest of them all."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:57.670738663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}